      "finding": null,
      "explanation": "The script writes PNG files to a caller-specified output directory without confirmation, guardrails, or safeguards (e.g., validating/creating the directory safely, checking for overwrites, limiting output count/size). In an automated or multi-tenant context, this can contribute to unintended filesystem writes, overwriting existing files, disk exhaustion, or writing to sensitive paths depending on how the surrounding agent supplies output_directory.",
      "remediation": "Add safety checks: (1) validate and sanitize output_dir (restrict to an allowed workspace), (2) prevent path traversal and symlink following if applicable, (3) check before overwriting existing files or use unique output subdirectories, (4) add limits on number of pages, total output size, and image dimensions, and (5) optionally require explicit confirmation or run in a sandboxed/temp directory.",
      "code_snippet": null,
