      "finding": null,
      "explanation": "Monkeypatching `pypdf`\u2019s internal `DictionaryObject.get_inherited` at runtime changes library behavior in a way that is not constrained to this task. If an attacker can influence inputs (PDF structure/field definitions) or the runtime environment, this kind of patch can cause incorrect parsing/field mapping, potentially leading to unexpected document modifications or bypassing validation assumptions.",
      "remediation": "Avoid global monkeypatching. Instead: (1) implement targeted logic without altering library internals, (2) if necessary, subclass/wrap pypdf components locally, (3) add strict tests on malicious/odd PDF form dictionaries, and (4) gate the patch behind a feature flag or narrow condition with clear invariants and revert behavior after use.",
